    <h1>Cross-functional R&amp;D Program Coordination</h1>

    <p>
      VL Consulting helps research-driven teams align priorities, clarify ownership,
      improve communication, and manage complex cross-functional dependencies across
      scientific, clinical, regulatory, and commercial workstreams.
    </p>

    <ol>
      <li>
        <strong>Misalignment Across Functions</strong>
        <p>
          Scientific, clinical, regulatory, and commercial teams often operate with different
          priorities, timelines, and definitions of success, leading to friction and slow decision-making.
        </p>
      </li>

      <li>
        <strong>Lack of End-to-End Program Visibility</strong>
        <p>
          Stakeholders don’t have a clear, unified view of progress, risks, dependencies, and timelines,
          making it difficult to anticipate delays or intervene early.
        </p>
      </li>

      <li>
        <strong>Unclear Ownership and Decision-Making</strong>
        <p>
          Critical activities fall through the cracks when roles, responsibilities, and decision rights
          are not clearly defined, especially across functions.
        </p>
      </li>

      <li>
        <strong>Poorly Managed Dependencies and Risks</strong>
        <p>
          Interdependencies between teams (e.g., preclinical → clinical → regulatory) are often
          under-coordinated, causing downstream delays and reactive firefighting.
        </p>
      </li>

      <li>
        <strong>Inefficient Communication and Meeting Overload</strong>
        <p>
          Teams spend excessive time in meetings without clear outcomes, while key updates and decisions
          fail to reach the right stakeholders at the right time.
        </p>
      </li>
    </ol>

  </section>

